# Code owners for review requirements.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
#
# `require_code_owner_reviews` was already enabled on main's ruleset and on
# the deploy gate branches, with no CODEOWNERS anywhere in the repository.
# GitHub requires a code owner review only for paths a CODEOWNERS rule
# matches — with no file, nothing matched, and the setting asked for
# nothing. It read as a second layer of protection and was not one.
#
# The catch-all is deliberate: every path has an owner, so no file can be
# merged without one. The specific rules below add nothing to the
# permission model today (same owner) — they are there so that adding a
# second maintainer later is an edit to those lines rather than a decision
# nobody remembers having to make.

*                       @goabonga

# The deploy surface. A change here decides what runs in an environment,
# not just what the code does.
/infrastructure/        @goabonga
/gitops/                @goabonga

# The pipeline itself: anything able to publish, sign, tag or deploy.
/.github/               @goabonga
/multicz.toml           @goabonga
/scripts/               @goabonga

# Packaging that lands on a host as root.
/packages/*/debian/     @goabonga
/packages/bdd/*/debian/ @goabonga
